you can just do:

> DT[J(letters[4:6]), list(v1=v1, 1),by=v3]

If you use `by` only the columns in it will be included in the output. But it seems like what you request is a nicer feature and I am for it. Because, when you just do, DT[J(letters[4:6]), sum(v1)] it gives you "v1". But when using `by`, it disappears. I find with your suggestion this would be more consistent.


Arun


